    ("Prepare recovery", "Before changing firmware, locate the correct chip, determine its voltage from its datasheet, and prepare a compatible external recovery method. Save independent complete reads and logs on a second device. Consistent reads are necessary but do not prove the right chip was read.", "https://libreboot.org/docs/install/spi.html"),
    ("Review prerequisites", "Read the board guide for vendor BIOS/EC prerequisites, CPU/RAM/GPU restrictions, flash layout and power sequence. Prepare OS recovery media, disk-encryption recovery keys and a compatible boot path. Do not update EC, Thunderbolt, or other controllers with the system ROM.", "https://libreboot.org/docs/install/"),
    ("Prepare the image", "Use an authenticated release for this exact target and the matching preparation procedure. Libreboot vendor-file injection and RBoot region-preserving installation are different workflows. A valid signature proves the publisher, not hardware compatibility.", "https://libreboot.org/docs/install/ivy_has_common.html"),
    ("External flashing handoff", "Use the board's disassembly and chip-location photos. Confirm pin 1, chip capacity, voltage, programmer logic levels and the documented power arrangement before connecting. Never combine target power and programmer VCC without explicit board-specific instructions. Stop on inconsistent reads. Multi-chip images need a reviewed chip-to-offset mapping.", "https://libreboot.org/docs/install/simplified-hw-flashing.html"),
    ("Internal flashing handoff", "Internal eligibility depends on both the board and its current firmware/protection state. Do not disable protections or force a mismatch merely because a guide for another system does so. This version withholds write commands until a reviewed board/release profile and its evidence requirements are implemented.", "https://libreboot.org/docs/install/"),
    ("Verification and recovery", "After a future approved write, require the programmer's verification and the board-specific completion sequence. If an internal write fails, do not reboot or power off casually: preserve logs and seek recovery guidance. A successful byte verification alone cannot prove the firmware will boot.", "https://flashprog.org/wiki/Flashprog"),
